{"schemaVersion":1,"releaseTarget":"ccmr-fidelity-v2.1-authentic-language","framework":"digitalSAT","domainId":"advancedMath","officialSkillFamily":"nonlinear functions","standard":"A.6C","status":"authored-pass-1","documents":[{"id":"mm_sat_A_6C_from-two-zeros_v21","active":true,"alignmentKeys":["texas:A.6C"],"alignments":[{"framework":"teks","code":"A.6C","role":"primary","evidenceLevel":"assessed"},{"framework":"digitalSAT","domainId":"advancedMath","role":"primary","evidenceMode":"direct"}],"assessmentContext":{"framework":"digitalSAT","examStyle":true,"domainId":"advancedMath"},"courseId":"algebra1","familyId":"mathmaster:sat:A.6C:from-two-zeros","familyVersion":2,"questionType":"response","activityRole":"practice","difficultyBand":3,"dok":2,"calculatorPolicy":"graphing","assessedConstruct":"A.6C","taskType":"createQuadratic","representation":"factoredForm","ccmrChallengeTier":1,"ccmrFamilyRole":"direct","ccmrAuthenticLanguage":{"version":"2.1","authored":true,"officialSkillFamily":"nonlinear functions","stemProfile":"from-two-zeros"},"prompt":"A quadratic function has zeros {{r1}} and {{r2}} and leading coefficient 1. Which equation defines the function?","generator":{"parameters":{"r1":{"type":"int","min":-8,"max":-1},"r2":{"type":"int","min":2,"max":9}},"derived":{"nr1":"-r1","nr2":"-r2","r1p":"r1+1","f1":"-r1","f2":"-r2","nr1p":"-(r1+1)"},"constraints":["-r1!=r2","f1!=0","f2!=0","nr1p!=0"]},"attemptFeedback":["Use the structure of the nonlinear relationship and the information given to determine the requested value or representation."],"supportHints":["Connect the equation, factors, zeros, vertex, or graph features that describe the same function."],"solutionReview":{"headline":"A zero $r$ gives the factor $x-r$: $f(x)=(x {{f1|signed}})(x {{f2|signed}})$.","reasoning":["Zero {{r1}} gives the factor $x-{{r1|paren}}=x {{f1|signed}}$; zero {{r2}} gives $x-{{r2|paren}}=x {{f2|signed}}$.","Check: $({{r1}} {{f1|signed}})({{r1}} {{f2|signed}})=0$ and $({{r2}} {{f1|signed}})({{r2}} {{f2|signed}})=0$.","With leading coefficient 1, $f(x)=(x {{f1|signed}})(x {{f2|signed}})$."],"commonError":"Using $x+r$ for a zero $r$: $(x {{r1|signed}})(x {{r2|signed}})$ has zeros {{f1}} and {{f2}} instead.","answerSummary":"$f(x)=(x {{f1|signed}})(x {{f2|signed}})$"},"assessmentItemFormat":"multipleChoice","choices":[{"id":"choice-d","label":"$f(x)=(x {{f1|signed}})(x {{f2|signed}})$"},{"id":"choice-a","label":"$f(x)=(x {{r1|signed}})(x {{r2|signed}})$"},{"id":"choice-b","label":"$f(x)=(x {{f1|signed}})(x {{r2|signed}})$"},{"id":"choice-c","label":"$f(x)=(x {{nr1p|signed}})(x {{f2|signed}})$"}],"responseFields":[{"id":"answer","label":"Choose the correct answer","inputProfile":"choice","expected":"choice-d"}]},{"id":"mm_sat_A_6C_leading-coefficient-from-point_v21","active":true,"alignmentKeys":["texas:A.6C"],"alignments":[{"framework":"teks","code":"A.6C","role":"primary","evidenceLevel":"assessed"},{"framework":"digitalSAT","domainId":"advancedMath","role":"primary","evidenceMode":"direct"}],"assessmentContext":{"framework":"digitalSAT","examStyle":true,"domainId":"advancedMath"},"courseId":"algebra1","familyId":"mathmaster:sat:A.6C:leading-coefficient-from-point","familyVersion":2,"questionType":"response","activityRole":"practice","difficultyBand":3,"dok":2,"calculatorPolicy":"graphing","assessedConstruct":"A.6C","taskType":"parameterReasoning","representation":"factoredForm","ccmrChallengeTier":1,"ccmrFamilyRole":"direct","ccmrAuthenticLanguage":{"version":"2.1","authored":true,"officialSkillFamily":"nonlinear functions","stemProfile":"leading-coefficient-from-point"},"prompt":"The quadratic function $f(x)=a(x {{f1|signed}})(x {{f2|signed}})$ passes through $({{x0}},{{y0}})$. What is the value of $a$?","generator":{"parameters":{"r1":{"type":"int","min":-6,"max":-1},"r2":{"type":"int","min":2,"max":7},"a0":{"type":"int","min":1,"max":5}},"derived":{"x0":"r2+1","y0":"a0*(r2+1-r1)","f1":"-r1","f2":"-r2","p1":"x0-r1"},"constraints":["f1!=0","f2!=0"]},"attemptFeedback":["Use the structure of the nonlinear relationship and the information given to determine the requested value or representation."],"supportHints":["Connect the equation, factors, zeros, vertex, or graph features that describe the same function."],"solutionReview":{"headline":"Substitute the point and divide: $a={{a0}}$.","reasoning":["Substitute $({{x0}},{{y0}})$: ${{y0}}=a({{x0}} {{f1|signed}})({{x0}} {{f2|signed}})$.","The brackets are ${{x0}} {{f1|signed}}={{p1}}$ and ${{x0}} {{f2|signed}}=1$, so ${{y0}}={{p1}}a$ and $a=\\frac{{{y0}}}{{{p1}}}={{a0}}$."],"commonError":"Dividing {{y0}} by only one of the brackets, or substituting a zero instead of the point.","answerSummary":"$a={{a0}}$"},"assessmentItemFormat":"studentProducedResponse","responseFields":[{"id":"answer","label":"Answer","inputProfile":"number","expected":"{{a0}}"}]},{"id":"mm_sat_A_6C_zeros-from-factored-equation_v21","active":true,"alignmentKeys":["texas:A.6C"],"alignments":[{"framework":"teks","code":"A.6C","role":"primary","evidenceLevel":"assessed"},{"framework":"digitalSAT","domainId":"advancedMath","role":"primary","evidenceMode":"direct"}],"assessmentContext":{"framework":"digitalSAT","examStyle":true,"domainId":"advancedMath"},"courseId":"algebra1","familyId":"mathmaster:sat:A.6C:zeros-from-factored-equation","familyVersion":2,"questionType":"response","activityRole":"practice","difficultyBand":3,"dok":2,"calculatorPolicy":"graphing","assessedConstruct":"A.6C","taskType":"interpretQuadratic","representation":"factoredForm","ccmrChallengeTier":1,"ccmrFamilyRole":"direct","ccmrAuthenticLanguage":{"version":"2.1","authored":true,"officialSkillFamily":"nonlinear functions","stemProfile":"zeros-from-factored-equation"},"prompt":"Which pair gives the zeros of $f(x)={{a|coef}}(x {{f1|term}})(x {{f2|term}})$?","generator":{"parameters":{"a":{"type":"int","min":1,"max":5},"r1":{"type":"int","min":-7,"max":-1},"r2":{"type":"int","min":2,"max":8}},"derived":{"nr1":"-r1","nr2":